      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "### CloudScale API \"Getting Started\" Guide\n\nWelcome to the CloudScale API! This guide will help you get started with integrating our REST API.\n\n#### Step 1: API Keys\nTo begin, you'll need an API key. Sign up [here](#) to generate your key.\n\n#### Step 2: Authentication\nWhen making requests, authenticate with your API key using this header: `Authorization: Bearer {YOUR_API_KEY}`.\n\n#### Step 3: Basic GET Request\nTo fetch data, use the following template:\n```bash\ncurl -X GET \"https://api.cloudscale.com/resource\" -H \"Authorization: Bearer {YOUR_API_KEY}\"\n```\n\n#### Step 4: Setting Up Your Environment\nEnsure your development environment is correctly set up:\n1. Verify your HTTP client library (e.g., `curl`, `httpie`) is installed.\n2. Set up credentials securely, such as environment variables for your API keys.\n\n#### Step 5: Handling API Responses\nUnderstand the response structure:\n- `200 OK`: Success\n- `401 Unauthorized`: Authentication failed\n- `500 Internal Server Error`: Server error\n\n#### Step 6: Error Handling\nImplement error handling in your code to handle different",
